    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented the daily owner creation limit:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitReachedException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when the day's quota is exhausted, mirroring the existing `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` style.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100` constant and a `rejectDailyLimitReached()` guard called from `addOwner` (right after required-field validation). It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and throws when that count is \u2265 100. Since the new owner isn't saved yet, it's never self-counted, so 100 owners dated today correctly rejects the 101st.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping the new exception to **`429 Too Many Requests`** with a `ProblemDetail` body consistent with the other owner-rule handlers.\n\nThe suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` creates 100 owners and gets 429 on the 101st.",
